# tv_menu_headless: the TV in-game menu and its input ownership, through the real App (headless, no ImGui).
# Run with:  virtualjaguar --headless --frames 30 --tv-test-script tv_menu_headless.txt
# (VJ_LIBRASHADER must point at a missing path when this script is run by hand, as cmake/VJTvTests.cmake sets it for ctest: a
# shader runtime would add a Picture row and the Down counts below would be off.)
# One event per line:  <ms> <verb> <args>.  <ms> is a script time; the gap to the previous line is the least real time
# that passes between the two (the hold arbiter reads the real clock).  Lines starting with # are comments.
#   load PATH            drop PATH on the window (the normal drop route)
#   key down|up|tap NAME a key event (SDL scancode name: F4, Escape, F8; "ctrl+L", "ctrl+shift+T" = with those held)
#   pad down|up|tap BTN  a button on the runner's virtual gamepad (SDL button name: a, b, dpdown, misc1)
#   mouse X Y           windowed only: move the real pointer within the main window (menu hover tests)
#   expect fullscreen=0|1 menu-pinned=0|1 menu-visible=0|1 (menu-visible needs a windowed rendered frame)
#   focus lost|gained    the window loses / gets keyboard focus
#   typing on|off        pretend a text box has focus (input.uiWantsKeyboard)
#   capture help|tvmenu  begin binding that action on the keyboard (the next key becomes its binding)
#   capture nav:INTENT   begin rebinding a menu button of the virtual pad (confirm back menu favorite start tabprev tabnext pageprev
#                        pagenext search): the next pad button becomes it (#1021).  expect cfg=...{padguid}... is its GUID.
#   tvsetting off|manual|auto  set the stored TV-mode setting and reconfigure (as Settings will); off = never, auto acts as manual
#   navdefault INTENT    the Default button of that menu intent of the virtual pad (back to the family's button, partner swapped back)
#   expect menu-open=0|1  paused=0|1  loaded=0|1  capturing=0|1  fast-forward=0|1  core-input=0|1  kb-bind=help|tvmenu:KEY
#   expect tv=0|1         TV mode is on
#   expect tv-screen=ID   the id of the TV screen on top (home, library, ...)
#   expect tv-owns-input=0|1  the TV shell has the pads and keys (0 while a desktop window covers the TV screens)
#   expect settings-open=0|1  the desktop Settings window is open
#   expect tv-more=0|1        it was opened by "More settings..." in TV mode: the pads and the arrow keys are its own (tv_more_settings.h)
#   expect home-visible=0|1   the desktop library is standing in for the game (never while TV mode is on)
#   expect library-window=0|1 the desktop Game library window is open
#   expect desk-pad=0|1       the desktop library owns the pads (#1021): TV off, no game running, no capture / desktop window, no mouse-opened popup
#                             (headless has no ImGui context, so that last part is covered by tv_ui_smoke)
#   axis NAME VALUE       set an axis of the virtual pad (SDL axis name: righty, lefttrigger; -32768..32767)
#   expect desk-scroll=0|1    the desktop nav holds a right-stick scroll (nonzero)
#   expect desk-pending=N     commands the desktop nav has queued (headless nothing draws the library, so they stay queued)
#   expect desk-popup=0|1     a library popup (tile menu, BIOS popup) opened from the pad is open and driven by it
#   saveconfig           App::saveConfig() (a headless run keeps its config in a private temp dir)
#   expect cfg=KEY:VALUE  the config holds KEY = VALUE; KEY:absent = the config has no such key
#   expect core-option=KEY:VALUE  the core option KEY reads VALUE (a session override, else the saved value: CoreHost::optionValueFor)
#   wait library         WINDOWED ONLY: block the script until the Library has scanned (not scanning, and at least one
#                        game); FAIL after 120 s.  The gaps of the lines after it count from the moment it is released.
#   shot PATH            WINDOWED ONLY: save the window as a PNG at the end of the next UI frame (that frame's TV drawing
#                        included).  Leave a gap before it for a screen change to finish animating.
#   quit                 WINDOWED ONLY: end the run through the normal teardown
#   (headless, wait / shot / quit fail their line with "windowed only": the Library is scanned by threads that only a
#   windowed run starts, and there is no window to save.  Windowed, any FAIL is printed and the script goes on.)
#   (core-input=1: the core would read some Player 1 pad button right now; the expect takes the snapshot itself)
# An expect first lets the per-frame input housekeeping run, so a fired hold has been handled by then.

# TV mode with no game (Manual): F4 turns it on and off; Esc at the root is not the shell's; Off ignores F4; Auto acts
# as Manual; a Share hold toggles it too.
0     expect loaded=0
0     expect tv=0
0     key tap F4
40    expect tv=1
40    expect tv-screen=home
60    key tap Escape          # at root: not the shell's
100   expect tv=1
100   key tap F4
140   expect tv=0
140   tvsetting off
160   key tap F4
200   expect tv=0
200   tvsetting auto           # acts as Manual in phase 2
220   key tap F4
260   expect tv=1
260   key tap F4
300   expect tv=0
300   tvsetting manual
320   pad down misc1
920   pad up misc1
960   expect tv=1
960   key tap F4
1000  expect tv=0

# Phase 2 never writes ui.tv_mode (a stored value would pin the default that Task 16 moves for nightly users); the
# remembered on/off state (ui.tv_manual_on) is still written.  Whatever the setting, the key stays out of the config.
1000  tvsetting manual
1000  saveconfig
1000  expect cfg=ui.tv_mode:absent
1000  key tap F4
1040  expect tv=1
1040  saveconfig
1040  expect cfg=ui.tv_mode:absent
1040  expect cfg=ui.tv_manual_on:1
1040  key tap F4
1080  expect tv=0
1080  saveconfig
1080  expect cfg=ui.tv_manual_on:0
1080  tvsetting auto
1080  saveconfig
1080  expect cfg=ui.tv_mode:absent
1080  tvsetting manual

# With TV mode on, Ctrl+L (File > Game library) opens the desktop library WINDOW (the home library is not showing: the TV
# screens stand in for it); with it off the home library is showing, so Ctrl+L only focuses its search box.  While the window
# covers the TV screens they take no pad input (RB would step to the Library section), and they get it back when it closes.
1080  expect home-visible=1
1080  key tap ctrl+L
1120  expect library-window=0
1120  key tap F4
1160  expect tv=1
1160  expect home-visible=0
1160  expect tv-owns-input=1
1160  key tap ctrl+L
1200  expect library-window=1
1200  expect tv-owns-input=0
1200  pad tap rightshoulder
1240  expect tv-screen=home
1240  key tap ctrl+L
1280  expect library-window=0
1280  expect tv-owns-input=1
1280  pad tap rightshoulder
1320  expect tv-screen=library
1320  pad tap leftshoulder
1360  expect tv-screen=home
1360  key tap F4
1400  expect tv=0

# "More settings..." from TV mode (#991): A on the last row of Interface opens the desktop Settings window and hands it the pad.
# RB x3 reaches Settings (Home, Library, Achievements, Settings).  With no game this session the core rows are hidden and Speed
# holds only its "Available once a game has run" line, so the rail is Picture, Speed, Sound, Interface (Down x3); Right enters the list: Show FPS, VSync, Theme, TV mode, More settings... (Down x4).
# While the window is open the shell has stepped aside (tv-owns-input=0) and the pad is the window's: a shoulder button that
# would change section does nothing, and B closes it (no popup, no active item), giving the pad back.
1400  key tap F4
1440  expect tv=1
1440  pad tap rightshoulder
1460  pad tap rightshoulder
1480  pad tap rightshoulder
1500  expect tv-screen=settings
1500  pad tap dpdown
1510  pad tap dpdown
1520  pad tap dpdown
1540  pad tap dpright
1560  pad tap dpdown
1580  pad tap dpdown
1600  pad tap dpdown
1620  pad tap dpdown
1640  pad tap a
1680  expect settings-open=1
1680  expect tv-more=1
1680  expect tv-owns-input=0
1680  pad tap dpdown              # the window's, not the shell's
1700  pad tap leftshoulder        # would step back to Achievements
1720  expect tv-screen=settings
1720  pad tap b
1760  expect settings-open=0
1760  expect tv-more=0
1760  expect tv-owns-input=1
# Esc closes it too (the focus is still on More settings...), and so does Ctrl+, -- which also ends the TV hand-off: the next
# Ctrl+, opens the plain desktop window.
1760  pad tap a
1800  expect tv-more=1
1800  key tap Escape
1840  expect settings-open=0
1840  expect tv-more=0
1840  pad tap a
1880  expect tv-more=1
1880  key tap ctrl+,
1920  expect settings-open=0
1920  expect tv-more=0
1920  key tap ctrl+,
1960  expect settings-open=1
1960  expect tv-more=0
1960  key tap ctrl+,
2000  expect settings-open=0
2000  pad tap leftshoulder        # back to Home (the shell remembers the section across TV mode off / on)
2010  pad tap leftshoulder
2020  pad tap leftshoulder
2040  expect tv-screen=home
2040  key tap F4
2080  expect tv=0

# Desktop pad navigation (#1021): the desktop library owns the pads while TV mode is off, no game is running and the home
# library shows.  A shoulder button is a mapped intent (SectionNext = next tab) and queues a command; TV mode on (or an edge of
# any ownership input) hands the pad to the TV screens and clears what was queued.
2080  expect desk-pad=1
2080  pad tap rightshoulder
2120  expect desk-pending=1
2120  pad tap leftshoulder
2160  expect desk-pending=2
2160  key tap F4
2200  expect tv=1
2200  expect desk-pad=0
2200  expect desk-pending=0      # the edge cleared the queue
2200  pad tap leftshoulder        # TV's, not the desktop library's: nothing queues
2240  expect desk-pending=0
2240  key tap F4
2280  expect tv=0
2280  expect desk-pad=1
# A binding capture owns the pad.
2280  capture help
2320  expect capturing=1
2320  expect desk-pad=0
2320  key tap Return             # ends the capture
2360  expect capturing=0
2360  expect desk-pad=1
# Start (Menu) is not the library's: it stays the app's and queues nothing.
2360  pad tap start
2400  expect desk-pending=0

# A right stick pushed while the library listens is a scroll; losing the pad (a desktop window opens, Settings here) or the
# window's focus zeroes it, so a stick let go meanwhile cannot scroll on.  Settings takes the pad while open.
2440  axis righty 30000
2480  expect desk-scroll=1
2480  key tap ctrl+,
2520  expect desk-pad=0
2520  expect desk-scroll=0
2520  axis righty 0
2560  key tap ctrl+,
2600  expect desk-pad=1
2600  expect desk-scroll=0
2600  axis righty 30000
2640  expect desk-scroll=1
2640  focus lost
2680  expect desk-scroll=0
2680  axis righty 0
2720  expect desk-scroll=0

# A game to play with.
2760  load @VJ_ROMS@/yarc.j64
2800  expect loaded=1

# F4 opens the menu (and pauses the game), F4 again closes it.
2860   key tap F4
2900   expect menu-open=1
2900   expect paused=1
2920   key tap F4
2960   expect menu-open=0
2960   expect paused=0

# A pause the player made is theirs: the menu does not undo it.
2980   key tap F8
3000   expect paused=1
3020   key tap F4
3060   expect menu-open=1
3080   key tap F4
3120   expect menu-open=0
3120   expect paused=1
3140   key tap F8
3160   expect paused=0

# F4 while a text box has the keyboard does nothing.
3180   typing on
3200   key tap F4
3240   expect menu-open=0
3240   typing off

# Esc is Back, and Back on the menu's first page is Resume.
3260   key tap F4
3300   expect menu-open=1
3320   key tap Escape
3360   expect menu-open=0
3360   expect paused=0

# A key let go while the menu is open still reaches the app (Tab is fast-forward and has to be let go of).
3380   key down Tab
3400   expect fast-forward=1
3420   key tap F4
3460   expect menu-open=1
3480   key up Tab
3520   expect fast-forward=0
3540   key tap F4
3580   expect menu-open=0

# A Share tap is not a hold: no menu.
# (`pad tap` presses and releases inside one line, so a stalled runner cannot stretch it into a hold.)
3620   pad tap misc1
3700   expect menu-open=0

# A Share hold of 600 ms opens the menu; letting go leaves it open.
3720   pad down misc1
4340  expect menu-open=1
4340  expect paused=1
4360  pad up misc1
4400  expect menu-open=1

# A Share hold while it is open closes it (the edge reaches the arbiter before the shell).
4420  pad down misc1
5060  expect menu-open=0
5060  expect paused=0
5080  pad up misc1
5120  expect menu-open=0

# Focus lost 200 ms into a Share hold: the hold is forgotten, so 700 ms later the menu is still closed.
5140  pad down misc1
5340  focus lost
6040  expect menu-open=0
6040  pad up misc1
6080  expect menu-open=0

# The menu holds the pause: F8 under it is refused, and closing gives back the state from before the menu.
6100  key tap F4
6140  expect menu-open=1
6140  expect paused=1
6160  key tap F8
6200  expect paused=1
6200  expect menu-open=1
6220  key tap F4
6260  expect menu-open=0
6260  expect paused=0

# The menu owns the input: with it open the core reads neutral input (under netplay the menu cannot pause the game, and this is
# what keeps it from playing under the menu); a button held across the close stays masked until released; with the menu closed it plays.
6280  key tap F4
6320  expect menu-open=1
6340  pad down dpright
6380  expect core-input=0
6400  pad up dpright
6420  pad down dpright
6440  key tap F4
6480  expect menu-open=0
6480  expect core-input=0
6500  pad up dpright
6520  expect core-input=0
6540  pad down dpright
6580  expect core-input=1
6600  pad up dpright
6640  expect core-input=0

# F4 while a binding is being captured binds F4 and does not open the menu.
6660  capture help
6680  key tap F4
6720  expect capturing=0
6720  expect menu-open=0
6720  expect kb-bind=help:F4

# Walk the menu with the pad (nine rows down: Save state, Load state, Achievements, Overlays, Settings, Controls, the TV-mode row, Reset, Close game): ask, answer No (back to the menu), ask again, Up to Yes (focus starts on No), answer Yes.
6760  key tap F4
6800  expect menu-open=1
6820  pad tap dpdown
6830  pad tap dpdown
6840  pad tap dpdown
6850  pad tap dpdown
6860  pad tap dpdown
6870  pad tap dpdown
6880  pad tap dpdown
6900  pad tap dpdown
6910  pad tap dpdown
6920  pad tap a
6940  pad tap a
6980  expect menu-open=1
6980  expect loaded=1
7000  pad tap a
7020  pad tap dpup
7040  pad tap a
7080  expect loaded=0
7080  expect menu-open=0

# TV mode survives a game: turn it on, walk to Library, start a game (the TV screen goes away under it), close the game
# from the in-game menu -- and the TV screen the player left is back.
7160  key tap F4
7200  expect tv=1
7200  expect tv-screen=home
7220  pad tap rightshoulder
7260  expect tv-screen=library
7260  load @VJ_ROMS@/yarc.j64
7300  expect loaded=1
7300  expect tv=1
7320  key tap F4
7360  expect menu-open=1
7360  expect tv=1
7380  pad tap dpdown
7390  pad tap dpdown
7400  pad tap dpdown
7410  pad tap dpdown
7420  pad tap dpdown
7430  pad tap dpdown
7440  pad tap dpdown
7460  pad tap dpdown
7470  pad tap dpdown
7480  pad tap a
7500  pad tap dpup
7520  pad tap a
7560  expect loaded=0
7560  expect menu-open=0
7560  expect tv-screen=library
7580  key tap F4
7620  expect tv=0

# A binding capture started with TV mode on keeps its input: the shoulder button that would switch sections (the screen
# the player left is Library: LB would take it to Home) and the Return key that would be Accept go to the capture instead
# of navigating.
7660  key tap F4
7700  expect tv=1
7700  expect tv-screen=library
7720  capture help
7740  pad tap leftshoulder
7780  expect tv-screen=library
7800  key tap Return
7840  expect capturing=0
7840  expect tv-screen=library
7840  expect kb-bind=help:Return
7860  key tap F4
7900  expect tv=0

# Ctrl+Shift+T (Cmd+Shift+T on a Mac) toggles TV mode with or without a game, whatever F4 is bound to; a game keeps running
# and the in-game menu stays shut.  It is ignored while a text box has the keyboard or a binding is being captured, and does
# nothing when the TV-mode setting is Off.
7920  key tap ctrl+shift+T
7960  expect tv=1
7960  expect menu-open=0
7960  key tap ctrl+shift+T
8000  expect tv=0
8000  key tap ctrl+T
8040  expect tv=0                # Ctrl alone is not the shortcut
8040  key tap shift+T
8080  expect tv=0
8080  typing on
8100  key tap ctrl+shift+T
8140  expect tv=0
8140  typing off
8140  capture help
8160  key tap ctrl+shift+T
8200  expect tv=0
8200  key tap Return             # ends the capture, if the shortcut did not already
8240  expect capturing=0
8240  tvsetting off
8260  key tap ctrl+shift+T
8300  expect tv=0
8300  tvsetting manual

# With a game loaded: the shortcut turns TV mode on and off, the game stays loaded and running, no menu opens.
8320  load @VJ_ROMS@/yarc.j64
8360  expect loaded=1
8360  key tap ctrl+shift+T
8400  expect tv=1
8400  expect loaded=1
8400  expect menu-open=0
8400  expect paused=0
8400  key tap ctrl+shift+T
8440  expect tv=0
8440  expect loaded=1
8440  expect menu-open=0
8440  expect paused=0
8440  key tap F4              # F4 with a game is still the menu, not the TV-mode toggle
8480  expect menu-open=1
8480  expect tv=0
8480  key tap F4
8520  expect menu-open=0

# A running game owns its pad: the desktop library does not, whether or not its window is open.  Paused with the window open it
# does again.
8520  expect menu-open=0
8520  expect desk-pad=0
8520  key tap ctrl+L
8560  expect library-window=1
8560  expect desk-pad=0
8560  key tap F8
8600  expect paused=1
8600  expect desk-pad=1
8600  pad tap rightshoulder
8640  expect desk-pending=1
8640  key tap F8
8680  expect paused=0
8680  expect desk-pad=0
8680  key tap F8
8720  expect desk-pad=1
8720  key tap ctrl+L
8760  expect library-window=0
8760  expect desk-pad=0
8760  key tap F8
8800  expect paused=0

# Menu buttons (#1021): Set captures the virtual pad's next button for a menu intent, and writes no game binding.  North (Y)
# becomes Confirm; Y was Favorite's, so the two swap (Favorite takes Confirm's old button, South).
8800  expect capturing=0
8800  capture nav:confirm
8840  expect capturing=1
8840  pad tap y
8880  expect capturing=0
8880  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.confirm:by
8880  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.favorite:ba
# Default on one half of the swap puts both back: no two intents on one button, and no stray key.
8880  navdefault confirm
8920  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.confirm:absent
8920  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.favorite:absent
# A reserved button is refused and writes nothing: the D-pad moves, so it cannot be a menu button.
8920  capture nav:back
8960  pad tap dpup
9000  expect capturing=0
9000  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.back:absent
# So is the button that opens the controls overlay (the pad's C_HELP, the touchpad button), as the TV-menu button is.
9000  capture nav:back
9040  pad tap touchpad
9080  expect capturing=0
9080  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.back:absent
# Esc cancels a menu-button capture without writing anything.
9080  capture nav:search
9120  key tap Escape
9160  expect capturing=0
9160  expect cfg=input.padguid.{padguid}.nav.search:absent

# A core option changed inside the in-game menu reaches the core once the menu is closed.  Down x5 from Resume is Settings (Save state,
# Load state, Achievements, Overlays, Settings), A opens the screen (the groups), Up x4 is Picture whatever group the Settings screen
# was left on earlier in the script (the shell remembers it), A opens Picture (the shader row is absent: the test rules the
# library out), Down x2 is Internal resolution (Integer scaling, Aspect ratio, then it), Right steps it from the core's
# default (1x) to 2x; B x3 is rows -> groups -> the menu -> Resume.  The write is a posted command: the value is read after the menu
# has closed and the paused core has had its boundary.
9200   load @VJ_ROMS@/yarc.j64
9240   expect loaded=1
9240   expect core-option=virtualjaguar_internal_resolution:absent
9240   key tap F4
9280   expect menu-open=1
9280   pad tap dpdown
9290   pad tap dpdown
9300   pad tap dpdown
9310   pad tap dpdown
9320   pad tap dpdown
9340   pad tap a
9345   pad tap dpup
9350   pad tap dpup
9355   pad tap dpup
9358   pad tap dpup
9360   pad tap a
9380   pad tap dpdown
9390   pad tap dpdown
9410   pad tap dpright
9430   pad tap b
9450   pad tap b
9470   pad tap b
9510   expect menu-open=0
9510   expect core-option=virtualjaguar_internal_resolution:2x

# "More settings..." opened from the in-game menu keeps the menu underneath and hands the pad to the window only.  Down x5 is Settings,
# A the groups, Down x4 lands on Interface (it clamps there, so the group the screen was left on does not matter), A its rows, Down x6
# clamps on More settings..., A opens the window.  The window's pad presses never reach the menu: two Ups and a shoulder button go to
# it, B closes it, and the menu is where it was -- the focus is still on More settings... (A opens the window again), and it takes
# two more B to leave the Settings screen and one to Resume.  Esc closes the window the same way.
9530   key tap F4
9570   expect menu-open=1
9570   pad tap dpdown
9580   pad tap dpdown
9590   pad tap dpdown
9600   pad tap dpdown
9610   pad tap dpdown
9630   pad tap a
9650   pad tap dpdown
9660   pad tap dpdown
9670   pad tap dpdown
9680   pad tap dpdown
9700   pad tap a
9720   pad tap dpdown
9730   pad tap dpdown
9740   pad tap dpdown
9750   pad tap dpdown
9760   pad tap dpdown
9770   pad tap dpdown
9790   pad tap a
9830   expect settings-open=1
9830   expect tv-more=1
9830   expect menu-open=1
9830   expect paused=1
9830   pad tap dpup
9840   pad tap dpup
9850   pad tap leftshoulder
9890   expect menu-open=1
9890   pad tap b
9930   expect settings-open=0
9930   expect tv-more=0
9930   expect menu-open=1
9930   expect paused=1
9930   pad tap a                  # the focus did not move: More settings... again
9970   expect settings-open=1
9970   expect tv-more=1
9970   key tap Escape
10010  expect settings-open=0
10010  expect tv-more=0
10010  expect menu-open=1
10010  pad tap b                  # rows -> groups
10030  pad tap b                  # groups -> the menu
10070  expect menu-open=1
10070  pad tap b                  # Resume
10110  expect menu-open=0
10110  expect paused=0

# A window that is no longer "live" is never left over a running game (its pad player could not close it, and the pads are the
# game's): a Share hold closes the menu under "More settings..." (the game unpauses and polls its pad itself), and the window goes
# with the hand-off.  Same walk as above to open the window, then the hold.
10150  key tap F4
10190  expect menu-open=1
10190  pad tap dpdown
10200  pad tap dpdown
10210  pad tap dpdown
10220  pad tap dpdown
10230  pad tap dpdown
10250  pad tap a
10270  pad tap dpdown
10280  pad tap dpdown
10290  pad tap dpdown
10300  pad tap dpdown
10320  pad tap a
10340  pad tap dpdown
10350  pad tap dpdown
10360  pad tap dpdown
10370  pad tap dpdown
10380  pad tap dpdown
10390  pad tap dpdown
10410  pad tap a
10450  expect tv-more=1
10450  expect menu-open=1
10450  pad down misc1
11070  expect menu-open=0
11070  expect tv-more=0
11070  expect settings-open=0
11070  expect paused=0
11090  pad up misc1
11130  expect settings-open=0

# A game dropped on the window while it is open from the Base layer: the game starts, the window goes (no game is left behind a TV-sized
# desktop window).  Close the game from its menu (Down x9 is Close game, A asks, Up is Yes, A answers), TV mode on, Base layer to
# Settings (LB x4 clamps on Home, RB x3), into the list and Down x6 clamps on More settings... whichever row the screen remembered.
11200  key tap F4
11240  expect menu-open=1
11240  pad tap dpdown
11250  pad tap dpdown
11260  pad tap dpdown
11270  pad tap dpdown
11280  pad tap dpdown
11290  pad tap dpdown
11300  pad tap dpdown
11310  pad tap dpdown
11320  pad tap dpdown
11340  pad tap a
11360  pad tap dpup
11380  pad tap a
11420  expect loaded=0
